    "1. Dumbbell hammer curl: the neutral grip lets you go heavier with less joint stress. Don't over-load and swing. Keep the elbow fixed, curl straight up and control the way down. The negative is almost twice as important because people neglect it.",
    "2. Seated alternating curl: start neutral, then supinate (palm up) past the knee for a stronger peak contraction. Sitting removes knee-bounce momentum. Squeeze at the top and don't swing with your back.",
